<title>GERMANY: German state NRW April CPI down 0.1 pct on month.</title>
<headline>German state NRW April CPI down 0.1 pct on month.</headline>
<dateline>DUESSELDORF, Germany 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>The statistics office of the German state of North Rhine-Westphalia reported the following consumer prices changes for April.</p>
<p>    Cost of living		    April	     March</p>
<p>    Mth/mth (pct change)	    -0.1		-0.2</p>
<p>    Year/year			   +1.6		+1.8</p>
<p>Note - These data are later combined with data from three other major German states to calculate the preliminary inflation figure for the whole of west Germany.  </p>
<p>The Statistics Office gave the following breakdown of its cost of living data:</p>
<p>						 Percentage change</p>
<p> Index/component			   mth/mth   yr/yr  Index</p>
<p> Without seasonal goods		  -0.2	1.7    115.7</p>
<p> Without heating oils &amp; Fuels	  -0.1	1.6    115.1</p>
<p> Without rental costs		    -0.2	1.1    112.3</p>
<p> Without service and repair	     0.2	1.4    113.8</p>
<p> Heating oil, motor fuel only	  -0.7	1.2    118.2</p>
<p> Service and repair only		 -0.8	2.3    120.2</p>
<p> Rents					  0.1	3.1    121.2</p>
<p> Household energy			  -0.1	1.1     98.5</p>
<p> Personal goods, services and other  -3.5	0.9    119.6</p>
<p> Transport and communications	   --	 0.3    115.2</p>
<p> Furniture				    0.2	0.8    111.6</p>
<p> Foodstuffs, drinks, tobacco	    0.5	1.0    110.5</p>
<p> Clothing, shoes			    0.1	1.0    112.7</p>
<p> Health and</p>
<p>  personal care items		     --	 1.4    115.3</p>
<p> Education, entertainment, leisure   -0.1	2.6    112.5</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
